12
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
James Bond 007: Everything or Nothing is a 2004 action adventure game developed by EA Redwood
Shores and published by Electronic Arts for the PlayStation 2, GameCube, and Xbox.

13
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:11,000
The game features a cast of voice actors including Pierce Brosnan,
reprising his film role as MI6 agent James Bond.

14
00:57:10,000 --> 00:57:16,000
Other returning actors include Richard Kiel, John Cleese and Judi Dench, as Jaws, Q and M
respectively, alongside Willem Dafoe, Heidi Klum, Misaki Ito, Shannon Elizabeth, and Mýa.

15
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:21,000
It is considered a continuation of Die Another Day (2002), featuring Brosnan and
Cleese in their final performances as Bond and Q, respectively.

16
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
Development of the game began in 2001.

17
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:31,000
Written by Bruce Feirstein, Danny Bilson, and Paul De Meo, Everything or Nothing
centers around Bond dealing with the use of nanotechnology as terrorism.

18
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
The player controls Bond, and the game includes several driving levels.

19
01:17:35,000 --> 01:17:41,000
It is the second Bond game played in third-person after Tomorrow Never Dies (1999),
and is the first Bond game to feature a two-player cooperative mode.

20
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
Everything or Nothing was released in February 2004.

21
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:51,000
It received "generally positive reviews" according to Metacritic.

22
01:29:50,000 --> 01:29:56,000
The film explores themes of cinema on cinema, filmmaking,
retrospective, british secret service, documentary filmmaking.

23
01:33:55,000 --> 01:34:01,000
The tone is uplifting and intense.
